A header line with text between HTML tags (`<b>Purpose.</b>`) is prose, and the header prints it, tags included; only a line of nothing but tags (`<p align="center">`) is markup that the header skips.
== args
input/d.rs
input/e.rs
== file input/d.rs
//! <b>Purpose.</b>
fn f() {}
== file input/e.rs
//! <p align="center"><img src="logo.svg"></p>
//!
//! Draws the logo.
fn g() {}
== stdout
input/d.rs (2 lines)
<b>Purpose.</b>
[L2-L2] fn f()

input/e.rs (4 lines)
Draws the logo.
[L4-L4] fn g()
== stderr
== exit 0
